{
  "meta": {
    "name": "Effects tour: footage",
    "description": "Chapter 8 of the effects tour: footage controls on generated clips (bundled photographs set in motion under a running clock). Fit blur, letterbox and cover with a focus anchor, a keyframed focus pan, a clip range, all five speed-ramp presets, a freeze frame with a flash and a B-roll cutaway.",
    "creativeDirection": "One footage control per beat, named in the corner. The running clock on the clip is the proof: ramps slow it down and speed it up, the clip range starts it at four seconds, the freeze stops it under a white flash. Review: no stretched frames, the pan eases at both ends, the clock reads every speed change and the cutaway returns on time."
  },
